{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"reddish-drinkable-canvasback","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observed (read-only over SSM, 2026-11-10 ~17:35 PST, host i-00880b2c7f13527c5)\n\n- Live MCP container `rebar-mcp-06b3b1a52303-8093` (image built at 06b3b1a5230, up ~23 h, healthy). Its env sets `REBAR_ROOT=MCP_CODE_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-code`, so the server reads `rebar.toml` from that workspace, not from the image's `/app`.\n- Workspace HEAD = `3835269d792` (2026-10-28 13:48 PDT). Its `origin/main` was fetched to `06b3b1a5230`; GitHub main is now `91182f96362`.\n- Running `LLMConfig.from_env()` + `resolve_model_string` inside the container resolves: default model `bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8`; `frontier` → opus-4-8, `standard` → sonnet-4-6, `trivial` → haiku-4-5. main's `rebar.toml` (after 3340 / `06b3b1a5230`) names the 5.5 models. **Production plan review is not running on the 5.5 models.**\n- `git status --porcelain` shows 27 staged entries. The index equals the tree of `e2ed08b343a` exactly (`git diff --cached --quiet e2ed08b343a` → 0), the working tree equals the index, there are 0 untracked files, and `e2ed08b343a^` = `3835269d792`. Index mtime 2026-10-28 17:47:28 PDT; last reflog entry is the 14:14 PDT fast-forward to `3835269d792`.\n- The entrypoint's `refresh_code_locked` refuses a dirty tree, so every restart since logs `mcp: dirty code checkout — refusing refresh` (first journal hit 2026-10-29 17:16 PDT). The refusal is stderr-only; nothing alerted.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven)\n\nThe state matches a fast-forward to `e2ed08b343a` that wrote index and working tree but never moved HEAD (process killed between the two). The killer is unidentified: the rebar-mcp journal has no entries in that window; autodeploy ran its 2-minute MCP reconcile throughout.\n\n## Impact\n\nEvery production gate that resolves config through this workspace uses the pre-3340 config: 4.x models, and any config key added after 2026-10-28. The 5.5 upgrade (and the Opus 5.5 refusal fix verification) is not live.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The production workspace is repaired by an operator-approved write and reports `0 0` against origin/main (runbook review-bot-ops.md \"MCP code workspace freshness\"); a fresh in-container resolution shows frontier/standard/trivial on the 5.5 ids.\n- [ ] The interrupted-fast-forward state (clean against a descendant commit of HEAD that is an ancestor of origin/main) is either recovered safely by the entrypoint or surfaced loudly (alarm/health), with a test reproducing the stuck state.\n- [ ] Root cause of the interruption identified or the evidence searched recorded.\n\nNo config key, env var or flag in the fix.\n","id":"6b02-067c-9dbb-47e7","parent_id":"9794-4336-5ed6-4561","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Production MCP code workspace stuck at 3835269d792 after an interrupted fast-forward, so plan review still resolves 4.x models"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1794362726608311101,"uuid":"c3c8075b-40fb-472b-a34f-b01bc42290e0"}